menu "Wii RA adapter"

config RA_LINK_USB
    bool "Console link over USB (TinyUSB vendor device) instead of EXI"
    default n
    help
        Build the adapter for the USB cable instead of the memory-card slot.
        The RA protocol is unchanged: ra_usb_link.cpp implements the
        exi_spi_slave.h API over a bulk vendor interface (VID:PID 303A:4052),
        so main.cpp handles requests exactly as on EXI. Needs the matching
        console side (d2x RAMOD built with USB=1, WiiFlow with USB support).

        The native USB pins (GPIO19/20) go to the console, so the log is on
        UART0 only (DevKitC "UART" port) and the USB-Serial-JTAG secondary
        console must be off (CONFIG_ESP_CONSOLE_SECONDARY_NONE) or the device
        never enumerates. Build with sdkconfig.usb.defaults (see README).

config RA_KEEP_ONLY_FIRST_SET
    bool "Load only the game's core achievement set (drop subsets/bonus sets)"
    default y
    help
        v0.27.6 cap: keep the first set of the patch, drop the rest (SMG:
        270 -> 161 achievements, ~40% less do_frame). Turn off to monitor
        every set (sdkconfig.allsets.defaults).

config RA_HARDCORE
    bool "Hardcore mode (leaderboards are only evaluated/submitted in hardcore)"
    default n
    help
        rc_client activates leaderboards ONLY in hardcore. Off (softcore), the
        leaderboards load but never run, so their per-frame cost is absent
        from any benchmark. The adapter is not an RA-approved client: use a
        test account (sdkconfig.hardcore.defaults).

config RA_LB_PROBE_ID
    int "Leaderboard probe: log this leaderboard's conditions (0 = off)"
    default 0
    help
        Diagnostic. After every evaluated frame, logs "LBP" lines with the
        leaderboard's state and, for each START alt and VALUE clause, every
        condition's current operand value, truth bit and hit count — on change
        (at most every 250ms) plus a 2s heartbeat. Use it when a leaderboard
        never starts/submits to tell wrong memory reads from unmet conditions.

config RA_COND_BUDGET
    int "Condition budget (0 = no cap)"
    default 35000
    help
        When the set's estimated trigger-condition count exceeds this, the
        most expensive achievements are dropped until it fits (never
        progression / win_condition ones), each drop logged. 0 disables the
        trim and loads everything.

endmenu
